1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:04,000
At the lunar south pole, the Sun and the Earth
both sit within a few degrees of the horizon.

2
00:00:04,200 --> 00:00:09,000
A ridge decides whether a site gets power.
Here the skyline is an input you can see and change.

3
00:00:09,200 --> 00:00:14,000
Every reading states its own model:
flat reference, edited mask, or imported profile.

4
00:00:14,200 --> 00:00:21,000
Eight published candidate regions, one window,
ranked by sunlit share, Earth visibility,
and the worst communication gap.

5
00:00:21,200 --> 00:00:26,000
The geometry is checked against NASA JPL Horizons,
and the residuals are published in the app.

6
00:00:26,200 --> 00:00:29,800
Pick a region. Pick a date. See the window.
